    "['family inet [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ipv4-family unicast', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nipv4-family unicast\\npeer 10.3.1.2 enable\\n##\\n\\nThe translation explanation:\\n1. \"family inet unicast\" in Juniper is equivalent to \"ipv4-family unicast\" in Huawei, which activates IPv4 unicast address family under BGP.\\n2. The neighbor-specific family configuration in Juniper translates to enabling the peer (neighbor) under the IPv4 address family in Huawei using \"peer X.X.X.X enable\".\\n3. Huawei combines these into a nested configuration structure where you first enter the address family context, then enable peers within it.', 'trans_template': 'ipv4-family unicast'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'peer 10.3.1.2 enable', 'parent_command': ['sysname CE3'], 'root': 'sysname CE3', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nipv4-family unicast\\npeer 10.3.1.2 enable\\n##\\n\\nThe translation explanation:\\n1. \"family inet unicast\" in Juniper is equivalent to \"ipv4-family unicast\" in Huawei, which activates IPv4 unicast address family under BGP.\\n2. The neighbor-specific family configuration in Juniper translates to enabling the peer (neighbor) under the IPv4 address family in Huawei using \"peer X.X.X.X enable\".\\n3. Huawei combines these into a nested configuration structure where you first enter the address family context, then enable peers within it.', 'trans_template': 'peer 10.3.1.2 enable'}]]": 1,
    "['neighbor [parameter2] family inet unicast', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'peer 10.3.1.2 enable', 'parent_command': ['sysname CE3'], 'root': 'sysname CE3', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\npeer 10.3.1.2 enable\\npeer 10.3.1.2 ipv4-family unicast\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Huawei devices, BGP neighbor activation and address family configuration are separate commands\\n2. \"peer X.X.X.X enable\" first enables the BGP neighbor\\n3. \"peer X.X.X.X ipv4-family unicast\" enables IPv4 unicast address family for that neighbor (equivalent to Juniper\\'s \"family inet unicast\")\\n4. Note that Huawei uses lowercase commands and \"ipv4-family\" instead of \"inet\" for the address family specification', 'trans_template': 'peer 10.3.1.2 enable'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'peer 10.3.1.2 ipv4-family unicast', 'parent_command': ['sysname CE3'], 'root': 'sysname CE3', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\npeer 10.3.1.2 enable\\npeer 10.3.1.2 ipv4-family unicast\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Huawei devices, BGP neighbor activation and address family configuration are separate commands\\n2. \"peer X.X.X.X enable\" first enables the BGP neighbor\\n3. \"peer X.X.X.X ipv4-family unicast\" enables IPv4 unicast address family for that neighbor (equivalent to Juniper\\'s \"family inet unicast\")\\n4. Note that Huawei uses lowercase commands and \"ipv4-family\" instead of \"inet\" for the address family specification', 'trans_template': 'peer 10.3.1.2 ipv4-family unicast'}]]": 1,
